hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to the  edition of ask Evan in today's episode  I'm going to answer question phone on my  face book readers Terry who wrote in  asking about partnerships and he wrote  in saying can you explain I want to sell  my brand and my hot wings who should I  partner with to market our product this  is a great question and partnerships are  a fantastic way to be able to reach a  new audience especially for when you're  starting the business it's a low-cost  way to be able to go out and get  customers so the idea here is find  somebody who's already selling to your  ideal target audience and strike up a  partnership with them so you can reach  that target audience a lot faster than  if you were going to go out and do  advertising or some of the more costly  or expensive ways to promote your  business so if you're selling wings or  it doesn't matter what type of product  is selling but in case of wings you want  to think about where are people going  and what are they buying before they buy  wings and after they buy wings so if you  think about before as an example what  are people doing where your customers  coming from before they buy your wings  if you don't have any customers yet if  you're just starting up think about  where your ideal customers are coming  from before they want to come and buy  your wings so example might be a little  league baseball maybe after Little  League baseball games everybody goes out  and wants to go have some wings so here  you want to make a partnership with  either the teams or other people sell  into Little League Baseball or the the  association or strike up deals with the  coaches so you can get them coming to  your your establishment after every game  they have maybe it's going to office  workers maybe people after after their  day at work they want to go home and buy  your wings because they want to have  dinner so it could be striking at  partnerships with the buildings where  these people are working or with the  individual company suppose flyers in  their in their own lunch room or their  photocopy room so you're thinking about  where are people going before they come  to you and let it know about you before  they have to make that decision and  partnering up with the companies who  also target those types  people in terms of how to make a  partnership arrangement there's a whole  you know lack of different ways to do  it's a million different ways to be able  to strike up partnership agreements but  the most common ones is either just  cross promotion so here it's you know  you're going to promote their product if  they promote your product and there's no  money changing hands so that can work  sometimes the second is you offer  commission so you're actually paying no  10-percent twenty percent thirty percent  whatever is depends on your business and  your margins if they're going to go out  and you know promote promote your  product quick example this and my first  software company this is what we did to  expand ourselves internationally and we  had a pretty good presence in North  America but also had people who could  use our software in Europe and Australia  and all around the world so we partnered  up with people who were already selling  to those companies and we gave them  Commission to help us sell it for us so  we've gave them even a few leads but  their job is to go and promote us to  their audience and so is great is we  didn't really have a foothold in England  or rest of Europe or Australia or you  know everywhere else around the world  and you just found people who are  already selling to those guys and made  an agreement with them to get them to  stop for us if you are giving them a  commission you want to think about  what's called the margin to motivate and  that's when you're you know thinking  about how much money do I have to give  them to really motivate them to sell for  me so if you're selling something and  you're giving them a one percent  commission you might say yeah okay let's  make a deal but they may not ever  actually sell anything for you because  it's not enough money to really make a  difference for them so think about for  your own business what you can afford  and how much is going to really make  them want to go out and sell so is it  ten percent is it thirty percent is that  fifty percent is it seventy-five percent  just depends on the type of business you  have and what your margins are a lot of  times people will will front load a lot  of these agreements so you get fifty  percent commission in the first year and  then that's it so if the type of  business where you get repeat customers  then you can afford to give up you know  a bigger percentage for the first  transaction in the first year then  ongoing then that's all your money  afterwards so that's that relationship  sometimes people  work out really effectively as well and  then the last way to do it if they're  know if you're not just going to do a  trade or if you're not going to give a  commission is you give a discount so if  you're going to companies or if you're  going to the Little League teams as an  example then you know they may not be  interested in taking a commission off  any sales made but you can give people  who they bring a discount so instead of  paying the commission that you'd  normally pay you give them a discount so  we said anybody who comes from this  company or from this little league team  you give ten percent off and you give  the middle coupon they can come in and  you know redeem at your place so that  could be an incentive for the company or  the little league team or whoever  partner to promote it to their people  because they're going to get a discount  for coming to your place so hopefully  that helps and get you thinking really  think about those people who are buying  you know or what are they doing before  they come and buy from you and how can  you target the companies who are you  know working around those people so  hopefully that helps if you guys liked  the video please give it a thumbs up I  love seeing them come in and it makes me  want to do more these videos for you so  thank you i always appreciate it and if  you have a comment or a thought about  partnership does love to hear it or if  you have a question that you want to ask  i'll definitely check out the comments  below so feel free to leave it in the  comments and we'll see you on the next  episode  you  you
 

